flowchart TB
    accTitle: GCVE BCP-02 disclosure lifecycle in Vulnerability-Lookup
    accDescr: Preparation uses role, email and intake settings. Teams receive, triage and verify reports in private cases and a review queue. Discussion, private notes and case status support investigation and testing. At release, the team publishes and links the vulnerability record and discloses the case. A CNA reserves a CVE ID and publishes through CVE Services. A GNA reserves a GCVE ID and publishes through its GNA source. Corrections, sightings, KEV and Insights support follow-up. New evidence returns to triage and lessons inform preparation.

    subgraph headings[" "]
        direction LR
        process["GCVE BCP-02 lifecycle"] ~~~ lookup["In Vulnerability-Lookup"]
    end
    subgraph preparation[" "]
        direction LR
        prepare["Prepare for reports"] -.- setup["Configure roles, email and intake"]
    end
    subgraph intake[" "]
        direction LR
        triage["Receive, triage and verify"] -.- review["Private reports and review queue"]
    end
    subgraph investigation[" "]
        direction LR
        investigate["Investigate and test protection"] -.- discuss["Discussion, notes and case status"]
    end
    subgraph publication["Publication and identifiers"]
        direction TB
        subgraph release_mapping[" "]
            direction LR
            release["Coordinate release and disclose"] -.- publish["Publish and link the record<br/>Mark the case Disclosed"]
        end
        subgraph authority_routes[" "]
            direction LR
            cna["CNA<br/>Reserve a CVE ID<br/>Publish through CVE Services"] ~~~ gna["GNA<br/>Reserve a GCVE ID<br/>Publish through the GNA source"]
        end
        release_mapping ~~~ authority_routes
    end
    subgraph followup[" "]
        direction LR
        monitor["Support users, monitor and improve"] -.- maintain["Correct records and review Insights<br/>Track exploitation with sightings or KEV"]
    end

    headings ~~~ preparation
    preparation --> intake --> investigation --> publication --> followup
    followup -.-> feedback["New evidence returns to triage<br/>Lessons inform preparation"]

